{
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Direct proportion says more → more.\n\nInverse proportion begins when a total is fixed. If the same wall must be built, more workers do not create more wall — they reduce the time.\n\nThe key question is not 'did a number increase?' It is 'what stayed fixed?'",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "24 workers finish a fixed job in 15 days. If the team grows to 30 workers, the job does not grow. The time must shrink.\n\nWorker-days stay constant: 24 × 15 = 360 worker-days.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "With 30 workers, days = 360 ÷ 30 = 12.\n\nThis is inverse proportion: workers rise by 30/24, so days fall by the reciprocal 24/30.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
